1
00:00:03,264 --> 00:00:04,874
[cell phone vibrating]

2
00:00:08,834 --> 00:00:11,011
[grunting]

3
00:00:11,098 --> 00:00:13,361
It's mine.

4
00:00:13,448 --> 00:00:15,798
[grunting]

5
00:00:17,887 --> 00:00:19,802
[Rigsby yawns]

6
00:00:19,889 --> 00:00:20,846
Rigsby.

7
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:22,413
[clears throat]

8
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,503
Oh, hey. Yep.

9
00:00:25,590 --> 00:00:27,505
You got it, boss.

10
00:00:27,592 --> 00:00:28,767
We're up.

11
00:00:28,854 --> 00:00:30,204
- Lisbon?
- Yep.

12
00:00:30,291 --> 00:00:32,902
Oh, no. No, she's gonna
call here next.

13
00:00:32,989 --> 00:00:35,992
- She'll know. Get out.
- Grace, wake up.

14
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:37,863
How is Lisbon gonna know
I'm with you, hmm?

15
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:39,604
Right, yeah.

16
00:00:41,954 --> 00:00:43,304
[cell phone ringing]

17
00:00:43,391 --> 00:00:45,436
Leave it.
Mm, no.

18
00:00:45,523 --> 00:00:47,438
- No.
- Get out.

19
00:00:47,525 --> 00:00:49,136
Get out.
Get out.

20
00:00:50,833 --> 00:00:53,140
Agent Grace Van Pelt.

21
00:00:53,227 --> 00:00:54,793
Hi, boss. What's up?

22
00:00:56,621 --> 00:00:59,059
Mm-hmm. Alright.

23
00:00:59,146 --> 00:01:01,452
[cell phone ringing]

24
00:01:05,152 --> 00:01:07,806
Bosco, and to what do
I owe this pleasure?

25
00:01:07,893 --> 00:01:09,112
You're up.
Where are you at?

26
00:01:09,199 --> 00:01:10,635
[Jane]
'Crime scene. Why?'

27
00:01:10,722 --> 00:01:12,246
Coffee run?
Usual for you, boss?

28
00:01:12,333 --> 00:01:15,640
Tall drip, black.
We need to talk.

29
00:01:15,727 --> 00:01:18,948
- About what?
- Come see me when you get back.

30
00:01:19,035 --> 00:01:20,602
Okay. Look forward to it.

31
00:01:22,647 --> 00:01:24,301
Hey, either of guys
heard from Hicks yet?

32
00:01:24,388 --> 00:01:25,737
No.

33
00:01:25,824 --> 00:01:29,045
Morning. Well, almost morning.

34
00:01:29,132 --> 00:01:30,699
[female #1]
'Good morning, everyone.'

35
00:01:30,786 --> 00:01:34,094
We got a Caucasian male,
50's. Gunshot to the head.

36
00:01:34,181 --> 00:01:37,706
[Cho]
'And tastefully garnished with
an explosion of yellow roses.'

37
00:01:37,793 --> 00:01:40,230
Security guard saw the body,
called Sac PD

38
00:01:40,317 --> 00:01:43,451
but this is a state cemetery,
which is why we're here at, uh..

39
00:01:43,538 --> 00:01:44,713
...Oh-dark-thirty.

40
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:47,150
Swell spot.

41
00:01:47,237 --> 00:01:48,499
[Cho]
'Check out the stippling.'

42
00:01:48,586 --> 00:01:50,632
'Looks like he was, uh,
shot at close range.'

43
00:01:50,719 --> 00:01:52,329
Yep. And fibers in the wound

44
00:01:52,416 --> 00:01:54,940
indicate clothes were
removed postmortem.

45
00:01:55,027 --> 00:01:57,421
- Hmm.
- What?

46
00:01:57,508 --> 00:01:59,031
You smell nice.

47
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:00,772
- Is that lilac soap?
- Yeah.

48
00:02:00,859 --> 00:02:03,297
- You got something, Jane?
- Uh, yes, I do.

49
00:02:03,384 --> 00:02:05,647
- Uh, he's naked.
- Let me write that down.

50
00:02:05,734 --> 00:02:07,649
Well, it makes him look
kinda sad, don't you think?

51
00:02:07,736 --> 00:02:09,129
Vulnerable.

52
00:02:09,216 --> 00:02:11,479
- 'A little comic, even.'
- Meaning what?

53
00:02:11,566 --> 00:02:13,263
He was posed like this.
He wasn't just dumped here

54
00:02:13,350 --> 00:02:14,830
willy-nilly.
This is a statement.

55
00:02:14,917 --> 00:02:17,049
Doctor, the mark on
the hand, is that a burn?

56
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:20,923
Looks more like
a freezer burn, actually.

57
00:02:21,010 --> 00:02:23,186
- Oh.
- Oh?

58
00:02:23,273 --> 00:02:24,622
That explains it.

59
00:02:24,709 --> 00:02:26,537
His liver temp is 45 degrees

60
00:02:26,624 --> 00:02:28,887
'but it's only around
58 in here.'

61
00:02:28,974 --> 00:02:31,716
So, somebody froze
his body in that position

62
00:02:31,803 --> 00:02:34,197
then dumped him here.
Could be a signature.

63
00:02:34,284 --> 00:02:36,417
Maybe a serial pattern.

64
00:02:36,504 --> 00:02:38,114
Lisbon and I will talk
to Bosco about that.

65
00:02:38,201 --> 00:02:40,290
See if he has any
similar incidents.

66
00:02:40,377 --> 00:02:41,465
Yeah, come on.
Let's get out of here.

67
00:02:41,552 --> 00:02:42,597
Let forensics
do their thing.

68
00:02:44,903 --> 00:02:46,905
You smell lovely.

69
00:02:46,992 --> 00:02:48,516
What is that?
Is that lilac?

70
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:52,868
Uh, yeah. Thanks.

71
00:02:52,955 --> 00:02:54,957
[Jane]
It's pretty.

72
00:03:02,356 --> 00:03:05,576
[Jane]
'Morning, Rebecca. They look
good. One of those for me?'

73
00:03:05,663 --> 00:03:08,536
You know, it's alright to like
me now. Your boss and I made up.

74
00:03:08,623 --> 00:03:10,668
It's okay, Rebecca.
I don't like him, either.

75
00:03:10,755 --> 00:03:12,757
She's a liar.
She loves me.

76
00:03:12,844 --> 00:03:15,369
'Yeah, keep tellin'
yourself that.'

77
00:03:15,456 --> 00:03:16,587
[screaming]

78
00:03:19,024 --> 00:03:20,287
[Lisbon]
'Oh, my God!'

79
00:03:20,374 --> 00:03:22,680
Oh, my God. No.

80
00:03:22,767 --> 00:03:25,292
[Lisbon]
'Sam! Sam!'

81
00:03:27,772 --> 00:03:28,904
He's gone.

82
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:34,518
- No pulse.
- 'Dyson's dead too.'

83
00:03:34,605 --> 00:03:37,260
[Lisbon]
'Jane, some help?
Get over here, now!'

84
00:03:40,132 --> 00:03:42,526
[Lisbon]
'Press as hard as you can.
Right, right there. There!'

85
00:03:42,613 --> 00:03:43,919
This is Special Agent Cho

86
00:03:44,006 --> 00:03:45,703
we've got agents
down on the fifth floor.

87
00:03:45,790 --> 00:03:47,792
[Lisbon]
Two, three, four..

88
00:03:47,879 --> 00:03:49,838
[Cho]
'Yes, inside the building.'

89
00:03:49,925 --> 00:03:51,666
We're in lockdown
on my authority.

90
00:03:51,753 --> 00:03:53,668
I have three agents down.
I need EMT's.

91
00:03:53,755 --> 00:03:56,148
'Roll SWAT, Sac PD
and CHP, and have them set'

92
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:58,238
up a perimeter.
Suspects may still be here.

93
00:03:58,325 --> 00:03:59,978
Just lock this
place down now!

94
00:04:02,764 --> 00:04:05,897
[Lisbon]
'Five, six, seven,
eight, nine'

95
00:04:05,984 --> 00:04:08,378
'ten, eleven, twelve,
thirteen, fourteen..

96
00:04:10,511 --> 00:04:12,904
[theme music]

97
00:04:20,738 --> 00:04:22,479
[instrumental music]

98
00:04:27,789 --> 00:04:29,181
[Lisbon]
'Hicks? Bosco?'

99
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:31,445
Bosco, Hicks.

100
00:04:31,532 --> 00:04:33,403
Stealing major crimes' food.

101
00:04:33,490 --> 00:04:36,667
Violation of penal code
section 484, I believe.

102
00:04:36,754 --> 00:04:39,975
- It didn't have a name on it.
- Uh, this one does.

103
00:04:40,062 --> 00:04:41,063
It's mine.

104
00:04:41,150 --> 00:04:42,412
It's from Cornaro's.

105
00:04:42,499 --> 00:04:44,458
Mm.

106
00:04:44,545 --> 00:04:46,851
Meatball sub's really
their best thing.

107
00:04:46,938 --> 00:04:49,550
You better hope I don't tell
Mandy you went off your diet.

108
00:04:49,637 --> 00:04:51,595
She's in New Hampshire
with her sister all week.

109
00:04:51,682 --> 00:04:54,990
Ah, there you are.
Agent Hicks, your form 41's.

110
00:04:55,077 --> 00:04:57,079
And, boss, the attorney
general's office called about

111
00:04:57,166 --> 00:04:58,907
the Armenian cartel thing.

112
00:04:58,994 --> 00:05:00,648
And you better hope
I don't tell your wife

113
00:05:00,735 --> 00:05:02,563
about you going
off your diet.

114
00:05:06,001 --> 00:05:07,176
[gags]

115
00:05:11,746 --> 00:05:13,225
Breathe, breathe.

116
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:15,358
Come on.
Breathe, breathe.

117
00:05:15,445 --> 00:05:18,143
I got this.
Clear!

118
00:05:19,841 --> 00:05:22,278
Okay, he's back.

119
00:05:22,365 --> 00:05:24,324
[male #1]
'He's bleeding out.
What do we got?'

120
00:05:24,411 --> 00:05:26,282
[female #2]
'There's no breath sounds
on the right side.'

121
00:05:26,369 --> 00:05:28,415
- His pulse is really weak.
- Run IV wide open.

122
00:05:28,502 --> 00:05:29,894
We're code 3.
Let's move.

123
00:05:32,288 --> 00:05:35,596
[indistinct chattering]

124
00:05:35,683 --> 00:05:36,814
You okay?

125
00:05:38,903 --> 00:05:40,296
What do we got?

126
00:05:40,383 --> 00:05:41,819
Lockdown's in full effect,
building-wide.

127
00:05:41,906 --> 00:05:43,473
Same with
the capitol and the DOJ.

128
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,388
Good, Cho's liaising
with the Sac PD

129
00:05:45,475 --> 00:05:47,085
they're setting up
a 2-block perimeter, now.

130
00:05:47,172 --> 00:05:48,826
Nobody gets in or out.

131
00:05:48,913 --> 00:05:50,175
All civilians
are being sent

132
00:05:50,262 --> 00:05:52,047
to the downstairs'
lobby for holding.

133
00:05:52,134 --> 00:05:54,354
SWAT's on their way up. We're
gonna do a sweep room by room.

134
00:05:54,441 --> 00:05:56,573
- Suspects could still be here.
- Get with security.

135
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:58,967
Check all the camera footage
and set up teams to interview

136
00:05:59,054 --> 00:06:01,491
all of the guards, janitors
and everyone down in the lobby.

137
00:06:01,578 --> 00:06:02,710
You got it.

138
00:06:04,712 --> 00:06:06,409
[Lisbon]
'He's gone. Go on now.'

139
00:06:10,065 --> 00:06:11,675
Jane?

140
00:06:11,762 --> 00:06:14,635
You may be in shock.
Look at me.

141
00:06:14,722 --> 00:06:18,029
There should be three bodies.
There-there's only two.

142
00:06:18,116 --> 00:06:22,033
- Where's Agent Hicks?
- I'll get Cho on that.

143
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:25,907
Lisbon, maybe we should
just wash up first.

144
00:06:25,994 --> 00:06:27,430
'Come on.'

145
00:06:28,779 --> 00:06:29,911
Come on.

146
00:06:34,132 --> 00:06:36,091
[water splashing]

147
00:06:40,356 --> 00:06:42,750
[intense music]

148
00:06:56,111 --> 00:06:58,461
[splashing continues]

149
00:07:01,377 --> 00:07:02,683
So, you never saw
Hicks this morning?

150
00:07:02,770 --> 00:07:04,728
No, I haven't seen
him since yesterday.

151
00:07:04,815 --> 00:07:07,122
And yesterday
was he angry or upset?

152
00:07:07,209 --> 00:07:10,908
You think Marlon Hicks
could have done this? Oh, no.

153
00:07:10,995 --> 00:07:13,476
We have to check
every angle, Rebecca.

154
00:07:13,563 --> 00:07:15,826
Let's back up.

155
00:07:15,913 --> 00:07:17,262
[Lisbon]
'When you went out
to get the coffee'

156
00:07:17,349 --> 00:07:19,264
did you see
anything unusual?

157
00:07:19,351 --> 00:07:21,049
Somebody who didn't
belong here, maybe?

158
00:07:21,136 --> 00:07:23,921
No. Everything was fine.

159
00:07:24,008 --> 00:07:25,401
It was normal.

160
00:07:28,970 --> 00:07:31,146
'God, I'm sorry.
I'm not helping.'

161
00:07:31,233 --> 00:07:34,062
Um, uh, I was gone
maybe ten minutes

162
00:07:34,149 --> 00:07:36,978
and I, I-I didn't
see anything weird.

163
00:07:37,065 --> 00:07:39,241
Bosco called the team in early
this morning, do you know why?

164
00:07:39,328 --> 00:07:41,504
Well, I thought that maybe it
was the Armenian cartel arrests.

165
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,595
You werethatclose
to making an arrest?

166
00:07:45,682 --> 00:07:49,643
Y-yeah, um, uh, there was,
um, a break this week.

167
00:07:49,730 --> 00:07:51,732
Um, an informant came
through, the boss said.

168
00:07:51,819 --> 00:07:54,778
It was something about,
um, um, um, a warehouse.

169
00:07:54,865 --> 00:07:56,606
[Jane]
'Uh, Lisbon.'

170
00:07:56,693 --> 00:07:58,478
Did forensics come up with
an ID on the frozen man?

171
00:07:58,565 --> 00:08:00,088
I haven't checked in with them.

172
00:08:00,175 --> 00:08:01,698
It's not really
a priority right now, okay?

173
00:08:01,785 --> 00:08:04,048
Okay. I guess.

174
00:08:06,355 --> 00:08:09,097
- You were saying?
- Camera four, also nothing.

175
00:08:09,184 --> 00:08:11,882
- Just an ordinary day.
- Weird, huh?

176
00:08:11,969 --> 00:08:13,754
- These guys are like ghosts.
- Yeah, no kidding.

177
00:08:13,841 --> 00:08:15,582
We checked the building top to
bottom. There's no sign of them.

178
00:08:15,669 --> 00:08:17,758
BFS are dusting every
stairwell and door for prints

179
00:08:17,845 --> 00:08:19,673
but it'll take days
to go through 'em all.

180
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:22,284
Lisbon said I should see
if you needed a hand here.

181
00:08:22,371 --> 00:08:24,025
Jimmy, go to
camera five now.

182
00:08:24,112 --> 00:08:27,202
[Grace]
'Lobby entrance,
same time code.'

183
00:08:27,289 --> 00:08:29,421
That's Rebecca coming back.

184
00:08:29,509 --> 00:08:32,076
She was gone nine minutes.
30 altogether.

185
00:08:32,163 --> 00:08:33,600
[Rigsby]
'I don't recognize
hat guy here.'

186
00:08:33,687 --> 00:08:35,340
Put him on the list
of people to check out.

187
00:08:35,427 --> 00:08:37,647
Okay, Jimmy, camera six.
The garage entrance.

188
00:08:37,734 --> 00:08:38,822
Mm-hmm.

189
00:08:38,909 --> 00:08:44,393
Hang on.
Something's screwed up here.

190
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,351
Some files are corrupted
on this data drive.

191
00:08:46,438 --> 00:08:48,223
Um, that's not possible.
Our firewalls--

192
00:08:48,310 --> 00:08:49,746
Have been breached.

193
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:52,575
Camera six and seven.
That's the garage.

194
00:08:52,662 --> 00:08:54,490
[Grace]
'They were disabled remotely.'

195
00:08:54,577 --> 00:08:56,100
Looks like at least
a 30 minute gap.

196
00:08:56,187 --> 00:08:57,406
Which means we have
no way of knowing

197
00:08:57,493 --> 00:08:59,060
who went in or out
via the garage.

198
00:08:59,147 --> 00:09:00,452
Jimmy, get somebody
from IT down here now.

199
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:01,976
Figure out what
we're dealing with.

200
00:09:02,063 --> 00:09:03,978
Okay, I-I'll tell my boss.

201
00:09:08,112 --> 00:09:09,897
Ten minutes.

202
00:09:09,984 --> 00:09:11,942
It was all over
in ten minutes.

203
00:09:18,993 --> 00:09:21,778
Okay, got it. Thanks, Avila.
I owe you one.

204
00:09:25,913 --> 00:09:27,958
Agent Lisbon,
I spoke to the governor.

205
00:09:28,045 --> 00:09:30,439
I told him that I have
my best team on this one.

206
00:09:30,526 --> 00:09:32,963
- I know you'll do us proud.
- Thanks, boss.

207
00:09:33,050 --> 00:09:34,922
I just reached out
to Sac PD narcotics

208
00:09:35,009 --> 00:09:36,401
about that
Armenian drug cartel that--

209
00:09:36,488 --> 00:09:38,403
In a minute.

210
00:09:41,015 --> 00:09:42,494
I just got word
from the hospital.

211
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:45,323
- He's not dead?
- No. No, Bosco's in surgery.

212
00:09:45,410 --> 00:09:48,239
But I wanted you
to prepare yourself.

213
00:09:48,326 --> 00:09:50,764
His injuries are
extensive.

214
00:09:50,851 --> 00:09:53,070
'Critical.'

215
00:09:53,157 --> 00:09:55,899
Teresa, I'm, uh, I'm sorry
to ask this, but I need to know

216
00:09:55,986 --> 00:09:58,249
that you're gonna be able
to go on with this case

217
00:09:58,336 --> 00:09:59,337
'no matter what happens.'

218
00:09:59,424 --> 00:10:01,731
If-if you can't,
just let me know

219
00:10:01,818 --> 00:10:03,167
and I'll put
someone else on point.

220
00:10:03,254 --> 00:10:05,735
Not necessary.

221
00:10:05,822 --> 00:10:08,477
You think Sam Bosco's gonna
let a little lead stop him?

222
00:10:08,564 --> 00:10:10,261
Please.

223
00:10:10,348 --> 00:10:12,089
I hope you're right.

224
00:10:12,176 --> 00:10:13,308
Good luck.

225
00:10:14,875 --> 00:10:16,267
Nothing on Hicks.

226
00:10:16,354 --> 00:10:18,182
I had a uni run by his house,
he's not there.

227
00:10:18,269 --> 00:10:20,141
- No car in the driveway.
- I've got something.

228
00:10:20,228 --> 00:10:22,317
You know that
Armenian drug cartel that Bosco

229
00:10:22,404 --> 00:10:26,016
was close to nailing? It's run
by a guy named Michael Assanian.

230
00:10:26,103 --> 00:10:27,061
Oh-ho, bad guy.

231
00:10:27,148 --> 00:10:28,410
Outside of the Mexicans

232
00:10:28,497 --> 00:10:30,151
biggest heroin distributor
on the west coast.

233
00:10:30,238 --> 00:10:32,675
Bosco must've spooked him. He
left the country three days ago.

234
00:10:32,762 --> 00:10:34,329
So, maybe he leaves town
to keep himself clean

235
00:10:34,416 --> 00:10:35,983
while his people kill Bosco.

236
00:10:36,070 --> 00:10:38,202
Yeah, makes sense.
Kill the team, kill the case.

237
00:10:38,289 --> 00:10:39,508
It's worth checking out.

238
00:10:39,595 --> 00:10:41,379
Lisbon, did we get
an ID on the man

239
00:10:41,466 --> 00:10:42,554
from the cemetery yet?

240
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:44,252
What's with you and this case?

241
00:10:44,339 --> 00:10:45,645
Oh, it's just a feeling.

242
00:10:45,732 --> 00:10:47,211
You think it's
connected to Bosco?

243
00:10:47,298 --> 00:10:49,300
- Maybe.
- 'How?'

244
00:10:49,387 --> 00:10:52,782
- Hard to say, I..
- Fine. Cho, call it up.

245
00:10:52,869 --> 00:10:54,654
'Forensics might have
posted something by now.'

246
00:10:54,741 --> 00:10:56,438
- Thank you.
- Run down this informant.

247
00:10:56,525 --> 00:10:57,874
See if he's got anything for us.

248
00:10:57,961 --> 00:10:59,397
Lauro in narcotics said
you could use his name.

249
00:10:59,484 --> 00:11:00,703
Yeah, will do.

250
00:11:00,790 --> 00:11:02,052
Forensics says cemetery guy's

251
00:11:02,139 --> 00:11:03,097
'fingerprints belong to'

252
00:11:03,184 --> 00:11:04,359
'a Dr. Towlen Morning'

253
00:11:04,446 --> 00:11:05,839
'age 55, Stockton.'

254
00:11:05,926 --> 00:11:07,057
Towlen Morning.

255
00:11:10,582 --> 00:11:11,714
Jane?

256
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:14,195
Cho, with me.

257
00:11:18,112 --> 00:11:20,505
[instrumental music]

258
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:51,101
[music continues]

259
00:12:18,738 --> 00:12:21,131
[music continues]

260
00:12:48,768 --> 00:12:51,161
[music continues]

261
00:12:56,036 --> 00:12:57,951
Oh, no.

262
00:12:59,082 --> 00:13:00,170
Hicks.

263
00:13:04,696 --> 00:13:07,090
[heavy breathing]

264
00:13:19,363 --> 00:13:21,235
How did you know
it was Red John?

265
00:13:21,322 --> 00:13:22,932
Towlen Morning was
the family doctor

266
00:13:23,019 --> 00:13:25,500
for Janet
and Carter Peak.

267
00:13:25,587 --> 00:13:27,719
Peaks were Red John's
third and fourth victims.

268
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:29,852
Carter presumed
to be the fourth.

269
00:13:29,939 --> 00:13:31,723
They never
found his body.

270
00:13:31,811 --> 00:13:33,464
That was nine years ago.

271
00:13:33,551 --> 00:13:35,162
Why attack the CBI today?

272
00:13:35,249 --> 00:13:36,859
Yeah, it's puzzling.

273
00:13:36,946 --> 00:13:38,513
I'm Red John,
why do I kill Morning

274
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,863
and Hicks
and attack Bosco's team?

275
00:13:40,950 --> 00:13:42,822
[Jane]
Carter and Janet Peak.

276
00:13:42,909 --> 00:13:45,346
Nine years ago.
Carter and Janet peak. Nine.

277
00:13:45,433 --> 00:13:47,783
Nine years ago,
I'm a lot less experienced.

278
00:13:50,133 --> 00:13:53,397
Something went wrong with Carter
and Janet Peak. A mistake.

279
00:13:53,484 --> 00:13:55,704
And he fixed it, but somehow
now, it's come undone.

280
00:13:55,791 --> 00:13:58,446
Hicks came to see
the doctor for a reason.

281
00:13:58,533 --> 00:13:59,621
He was checking
something out.

282
00:13:59,708 --> 00:14:01,057
Red John killed him for it.

283
00:14:01,144 --> 00:14:02,319
Killed them all.

284
00:14:02,406 --> 00:14:04,626
Except for Bosco, I mean.

285
00:14:04,713 --> 00:14:06,236
Bosco had a lead in the Red John
case.

286
00:14:06,323 --> 00:14:08,282
Cho, go inside,
check the doctor's files

287
00:14:08,369 --> 00:14:09,936
for Carter and Janet Peak.

288
00:14:10,023 --> 00:14:12,895
X-rays, labs, everything.

289
00:14:12,982 --> 00:14:16,116
Why did Bosco want
the medical reports?

290
00:14:16,203 --> 00:14:18,205
What did he know?

291
00:14:18,292 --> 00:14:20,120
He's in ICU
in a medically induced coma.

292
00:14:20,207 --> 00:14:21,556
He's not gonna
tell us anything.

293
00:14:21,643 --> 00:14:24,472
- I know. I know.
- The case files will.

294
00:14:26,822 --> 00:14:28,998
Van Pelt, have BFS
search Bosco's office

295
00:14:29,085 --> 00:14:31,479
for any new evidence
or notes in the Red John file.

296
00:14:31,566 --> 00:14:35,526
And you and Rigsby start working
with the secretary, Rebecca.

297
00:14:35,613 --> 00:14:36,701
Mm-hmm.

298
00:14:42,185 --> 00:14:44,579
[instrumental music]

299
00:14:56,896 --> 00:15:00,073
Hey, boss.
Nothing from Rebecca.

300
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:01,683
The BFS techs are
still taking apart

301
00:15:01,770 --> 00:15:03,293
Bosco's office, but so far--

302
00:15:03,380 --> 00:15:04,904
- Is Jane back?
- 'I haven't seen him.'

303
00:15:04,991 --> 00:15:06,818
- Find him, would you?
- Yeah.

304
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:09,560
[Minelli]
'Special Agents
Nick Martinez and Mark Dyson'

305
00:15:09,647 --> 00:15:12,607
'died at the scene here.'

306
00:15:12,694 --> 00:15:14,304
And Special Agent Marlon Hicks

307
00:15:14,391 --> 00:15:18,265
was found dead
at a secondary crime scene.

308
00:15:18,352 --> 00:15:22,486
Special Agent Samuel Bosco
remains in critical condition.

309
00:15:22,573 --> 00:15:25,141
We are devoting every resource
to this investigation.

310
00:15:25,228 --> 00:15:28,753
And I promise, I promise
the agents' families

311
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,626
we will not rest..

312
00:15:31,713 --> 00:15:34,324
...till we bring
the perpetrator to justice.

313
00:15:34,411 --> 00:15:37,197
Special Agent Minelli,
our condolences.

314
00:15:37,284 --> 00:15:40,940
Would you describe your
feelings at this terrible time?

315
00:15:41,027 --> 00:15:44,247
Wow, Meredith, that..

316
00:15:44,334 --> 00:15:46,249
You media guys,
that's just dis..

317
00:15:50,384 --> 00:15:52,386
You know, for eight years

318
00:15:52,473 --> 00:15:55,128
I've put up with the idiotic
questions of the media

319
00:15:55,215 --> 00:15:57,782
and I've never said squat.

320
00:15:57,869 --> 00:16:02,570
But today, I must
tell you, Meredith..

321
00:16:02,657 --> 00:16:06,748
...you've really set a new
standard in horse's assery.

322
00:16:10,186 --> 00:16:16,062
You people have
no conceptof what we do.

323
00:16:16,149 --> 00:16:18,934
We go into dark,
horrible places

324
00:16:19,021 --> 00:16:22,111
alone and afraid

325
00:16:22,198 --> 00:16:23,852
'and we do it with no money'

326
00:16:23,939 --> 00:16:26,376
with broken-down vehicles with..

327
00:16:26,463 --> 00:16:28,988
...computers that have
more viruses than a $10 whore.

328
00:16:30,598 --> 00:16:33,427
How? Good people.

329
00:16:35,342 --> 00:16:38,649
And I lost three
good people today

330
00:16:38,736 --> 00:16:40,912
and a fourth who's
in critical condition

331
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,393
and you ask me
how I'm feeling.

332
00:16:45,482 --> 00:16:48,181
I'm feelingsad..

333
00:16:48,268 --> 00:16:50,835
...you...moron.

334
00:16:54,796 --> 00:16:55,927
Any other questions?

335
00:16:58,974 --> 00:17:02,499
Okay, then.
Good day to you.

336
00:17:02,586 --> 00:17:04,371
Elizabeth, carry on.

337
00:17:08,723 --> 00:17:09,898
Virgil.

338
00:17:11,508 --> 00:17:14,250
Horse's assery? Nice.

339
00:17:14,337 --> 00:17:15,686
They shouldn't
have done that.

340
00:17:15,773 --> 00:17:17,993
Hey, you told them the truth.

341
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:19,212
I did.

342
00:17:20,474 --> 00:17:21,562
Felt good.

343
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:26,045
Stick with us, boss.
We need you.

344
00:17:26,132 --> 00:17:29,309
Okay. Yes.

345
00:17:29,396 --> 00:17:30,832
I gotta run. You got this?

346
00:17:31,572 --> 00:17:32,747
Go.

347
00:17:37,708 --> 00:17:40,059
[indistinct chattering]

348
00:17:48,763 --> 00:17:49,938
Evening, gentlemen.

349
00:18:00,470 --> 00:18:01,645
- Hi.
- Hi.

350
00:18:01,732 --> 00:18:04,344
- You are?
- Oh, I'm sorry. Uh..

351
00:18:04,431 --> 00:18:06,911
Patrick Jane, CBI.
I'm a friend of his.

352
00:18:06,998 --> 00:18:10,306
- 'Uh, how's he doing?'
- He's not good.

353
00:18:10,393 --> 00:18:12,265
The next two days
should tell us a lot.

354
00:18:12,352 --> 00:18:15,659
Oh, he was in such pain.
Is he getting enough morphine?

355
00:18:15,746 --> 00:18:16,834
He should be.

356
00:18:20,011 --> 00:18:21,796
Looks good. Call me if
you need anything else.

357
00:18:21,883 --> 00:18:23,754
Will do. Thanks, doc.

358
00:18:32,894 --> 00:18:34,330
[Lisbon]
'What are you doing?'

359
00:18:36,419 --> 00:18:38,247
Unplugging his morphine.

360
00:18:38,334 --> 00:18:40,858
I'd ask a doctor to do it, but
I think I know what they'd say.

361
00:18:40,945 --> 00:18:43,470
- Are you crazy?
- 'Yes.'

362
00:18:43,557 --> 00:18:45,776
That's exactly
what they'd say.

363
00:18:45,863 --> 00:18:47,996
They wouldn't understand
the moral imperative here.

364
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:52,348
Bosco is the only person

365
00:18:52,435 --> 00:18:55,351
that can tell us what
he found on Red John.

366
00:18:55,438 --> 00:18:58,224
And he may die,
we need to wake him up

367
00:18:58,311 --> 00:19:01,879
and have him tell us everything
he knows while he still can.

368
00:19:01,966 --> 00:19:04,360
[machine beeping]

369
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:13,108
- Y-you can't do that.
- Why not?

370
00:19:13,195 --> 00:19:14,892
Morphine doesn't
make him any better.

371
00:19:14,979 --> 00:19:18,374
- It just stops the pain.
- Yes, that's what it does.

372
00:19:18,461 --> 00:19:21,334
Pain is nothing.
Pain means he's still alive.

373
00:19:21,421 --> 00:19:23,988
We need him now,
Lisbon.Now.

374
00:19:24,075 --> 00:19:25,729
He's useless to us
when he's dead.

375
00:19:25,816 --> 00:19:30,430
- Shut up! He's gonna live.
- Maybe and maybe not.

376
00:19:30,517 --> 00:19:32,432
- God, you're a cold bastard.
- Oh, please.

377
00:19:32,519 --> 00:19:35,217
Y-y-you need
to think logically.

378
00:19:35,304 --> 00:19:37,176
He would want
us to do this.

379
00:19:37,263 --> 00:19:39,787
How could you know what he would
want? You don't even know him.

380
00:19:39,874 --> 00:19:42,790
But you do, if he had
to suffer pain to stop Red John

381
00:19:42,877 --> 00:19:46,097
he would do that. You know
that he would. You know that.

382
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:48,665
What's all the commotion?
What the..

383
00:19:48,752 --> 00:19:50,145
Did you touch that machine?

384
00:19:51,755 --> 00:19:52,930
No.

385
00:20:00,677 --> 00:20:03,158
[Minelli on TV]
'Good people.'

386
00:20:03,245 --> 00:20:07,075
And I've lost three
good people today..

387
00:20:08,990 --> 00:20:10,687
[Grace]
'Is Lisbon with you?'

388
00:20:10,774 --> 00:20:11,949
No.

389
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:15,344
What's going on?

390
00:20:15,431 --> 00:20:18,304
We got a hit...on Bosco's
cell phone records.

391
00:20:18,391 --> 00:20:19,914
Just before the attack
Bosco called a cop

392
00:20:20,001 --> 00:20:22,438
down in Cloverville,
not far from Stockton.

393
00:20:22,525 --> 00:20:24,310
Cop told me when they
tore down an old strip mall

394
00:20:24,397 --> 00:20:26,660
last week, they found a body
buried in the foundation.

395
00:20:26,747 --> 00:20:27,791
Body?

396
00:20:27,878 --> 00:20:29,053
The cop who posted the bulletin

397
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:30,316
said he got a call from Bosco

398
00:20:30,403 --> 00:20:31,752
saying he'd go
and check it out.

399
00:20:31,839 --> 00:20:33,536
What body?

400
00:20:33,623 --> 00:20:35,146
This one.

401
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:37,410
Cloverville PD
e-mailed a copy of the x-rays.

402
00:20:37,497 --> 00:20:39,238
John Doe, 30's.

403
00:20:39,325 --> 00:20:42,589
See here? His head was
almost cut off. Vicious.

404
00:20:42,676 --> 00:20:45,940
- Then there's this.
- What's that?

405
00:20:46,027 --> 00:20:48,072
- 'His leg.'
- He's missing a leg?

406
00:20:48,159 --> 00:20:50,292
The coroner told the cop
it was not part of the attack.

407
00:20:50,379 --> 00:20:53,077
A much earlier amputation,
he said. Distinctive.

408
00:20:53,164 --> 00:20:55,210
The files we got from
Dr. Morning's office

409
00:20:55,297 --> 00:20:57,081
this matches an x-ray
we found there.

410
00:20:57,168 --> 00:20:59,736
Carter Peak.
Carter Peak, retired army

411
00:20:59,823 --> 00:21:01,999
lost his right leg
during the First Gulf War.

412
00:21:02,086 --> 00:21:03,566
They found the missing
Red John victim.

413
00:21:03,653 --> 00:21:05,612
Better still.

414
00:21:05,699 --> 00:21:07,744
This is Red John's mistake.

415
00:21:07,831 --> 00:21:11,008
This is it. He made
a mistake and this is it.

416
00:21:23,194 --> 00:21:25,371
[Jane narrating]
Killing Carter Peak
wasn't Red John's MO.

417
00:21:25,458 --> 00:21:27,416
He was a man who was
killed with his wife.

418
00:21:27,503 --> 00:21:29,244
His body was removed
from the scene.

419
00:21:29,331 --> 00:21:31,855
It is unlike any of Red John's 14 other murders.

420
00:21:31,942 --> 00:21:34,684
Maybe, Carter
returned unexpectedly

421
00:21:34,771 --> 00:21:36,338
maybe, there was a struggle.

422
00:21:36,425 --> 00:21:37,905
[Jane]
'So, Peak's body resurfaces.'

423
00:21:37,992 --> 00:21:41,735
Red John hears about it somehow,
and it upsets him.

424
00:21:41,822 --> 00:21:44,955
A, how does he
hear about the body?

425
00:21:45,042 --> 00:21:47,697
Off the bulletin, I guess.
It was statewide.

426
00:21:47,784 --> 00:21:50,004
And B, why does it upset him?

427
00:21:50,091 --> 00:21:51,745
There's evidence on
Carter Peak's body.

428
00:21:51,832 --> 00:21:53,181
That's why he tried
to make it disappear.

429
00:21:53,268 --> 00:21:56,489
Damning evidence, like DNA.

430
00:21:56,576 --> 00:21:58,186
We gotta get to Cloverville.

431
00:22:01,755 --> 00:22:04,105
The cement matrix preserved
the body remarkably well.

432
00:22:04,192 --> 00:22:06,194
We were able to run
a full DNA crime kit.

433
00:22:06,281 --> 00:22:08,457
Hair, skin under
the fingernails, etcetera.

434
00:22:08,544 --> 00:22:10,329
We need someone
sitting on this place 24/7

435
00:22:10,416 --> 00:22:12,287
until we can move
the body up to Sacramento.

436
00:22:22,036 --> 00:22:24,038
Whoops.
Uh, my bad.

437
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:29,826
Wow!

438
00:22:29,913 --> 00:22:31,524
That's weird.

439
00:22:31,611 --> 00:22:34,614
Yeah, it is.
Where's the body, doc?

440
00:22:34,701 --> 00:22:37,007
Uh, let me,
let me check the log here.

441
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:44,798
Okay, you guys
gotta get your signals

442
00:22:44,885 --> 00:22:46,669
straightened up in Sacramento.

443
00:22:46,756 --> 00:22:48,541
CBI already picked up
the body night before last.

444
00:22:48,628 --> 00:22:49,846
- CBI did?
- Yeah.

445
00:22:49,933 --> 00:22:52,196
Night shift logged it,
right here.

446
00:22:52,283 --> 00:22:55,461
California Bureau
of Investigation, an Agent Rojo.

447
00:22:55,548 --> 00:22:56,853
The body, samples.

448
00:22:56,940 --> 00:22:58,681
Uh, everything we had,
it looks like.

449
00:22:58,768 --> 00:22:59,943
See for yourself.

450
00:23:01,292 --> 00:23:03,512
Arrived at 2:15 a.m.
with a meat wagon.

451
00:23:03,599 --> 00:23:05,166
The night before the CBI attack.

452
00:23:05,253 --> 00:23:07,473
I can get you photos, though.
We usually keep a set.

453
00:23:07,560 --> 00:23:09,431
But the crime scene kit,
the DNA samples..

454
00:23:09,518 --> 00:23:11,651
- What about the DNA?
- Well, I'm telling ya.

455
00:23:11,738 --> 00:23:13,783
I-it should have all gone with
your guy. That's procedure.

456
00:23:13,870 --> 00:23:15,655
He wasn't our guy.
Red John?

457
00:23:15,742 --> 00:23:17,221
Call in your night shift person.

458
00:23:17,308 --> 00:23:19,136
I-it's important that we get
an idea of what this, uh..

459
00:23:19,223 --> 00:23:20,790
...Agent Rojo looks like.

460
00:23:24,533 --> 00:23:25,621
[knock on door]

461
00:23:25,708 --> 00:23:27,101
You wanted to see me, boss?

462
00:23:27,188 --> 00:23:28,624
Sit down, please.

463
00:23:30,757 --> 00:23:34,021
Bosco's doing better.
I talked to his doctor.

464
00:23:34,108 --> 00:23:35,892
Good.

465
00:23:35,979 --> 00:23:37,111
That's good.

466
00:23:38,547 --> 00:23:40,723
You okay, boss?

467
00:23:40,810 --> 00:23:42,377
Is this about before
at the press conference?

468
00:23:42,464 --> 00:23:43,465
No.

469
00:23:45,249 --> 00:23:46,294
Yes.

470
00:23:47,382 --> 00:23:48,427
I, um..

471
00:23:50,472 --> 00:23:54,650
I have something to tell you,
Teresa. Something important.

472
00:23:54,737 --> 00:23:58,349
[knock on door]
What is it, agent?

473
00:23:58,437 --> 00:24:00,439
Sorry to interrupt
but I've been going through

474
00:24:00,526 --> 00:24:04,138
the security footage, trying to
ID everyone going in and out.

475
00:24:04,225 --> 00:24:05,313
[Grace]
'This is time coded
for this morning'

476
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:07,054
'right before the attack.'

477
00:24:07,141 --> 00:24:10,536
'According to employee support
services, that's Amblyn Demott.'

478
00:24:10,623 --> 00:24:12,451
'An analyst on four.'

479
00:24:12,538 --> 00:24:13,930
So what?

480
00:24:14,017 --> 00:24:16,193
Demott went on
maternity leave last month.

481
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:18,108
She had her baby yesterday.

482
00:24:18,195 --> 00:24:21,547
'There's no way she could be
where that camera says she was.'

483
00:24:21,634 --> 00:24:23,897
Someone switched the footage.

484
00:24:23,984 --> 00:24:26,160
We can't trust
anything on any camera.

485
00:24:29,511 --> 00:24:31,948
[Cho]
'You transferred the body
to the custody of a CBI agent?'

486
00:24:32,035 --> 00:24:34,516
- Yeah.
- 'Describe this agent.'

487
00:24:34,603 --> 00:24:39,042
Dark hair, not that tall,
kinda dumpy, olive-complected.

488
00:24:39,129 --> 00:24:41,131
Wore these heel that clicked.

489
00:24:41,218 --> 00:24:42,611
[Cho]
'A woman?'

490
00:24:42,698 --> 00:24:45,658
Wore a thing, a...
what's it, in her hair.

491
00:24:45,745 --> 00:24:48,269
- A Barrette.
- 'Right. Barrette.'

492
00:24:56,146 --> 00:24:57,844
Hey, sweetie.

493
00:24:57,931 --> 00:24:59,976
Okay.

494
00:25:00,063 --> 00:25:01,369
Here you go.
That's for you.

495
00:25:01,456 --> 00:25:03,458
- Have a nice day.
- Thank you.

496
00:25:05,808 --> 00:25:07,244
- Hi, Rich.
- Hi.

497
00:25:11,335 --> 00:25:13,686
- Hello, Barney. How you doing?
- Hey, Rebecca.

498
00:25:22,216 --> 00:25:24,566
[ECG machine beeping]

499
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:28,396
[whispering]
Hey, boss.

500
00:25:28,483 --> 00:25:30,659
Boss? Hey.

501
00:25:33,053 --> 00:25:35,446
[intense music]

502
00:25:47,154 --> 00:25:48,895
[Dyson]
'Weren't you heading
to Cloverville?'

503
00:25:48,982 --> 00:25:52,420
Uh, as soon as I brief Jane.

504
00:25:52,507 --> 00:25:55,292
Samuel Bosco Jr.
getting soft.

505
00:25:55,379 --> 00:25:57,730
- 'Hey!'
- Screw you, Martinez.

506
00:25:57,817 --> 00:25:59,906
Hey, guys.
Look what I have.

507
00:25:59,993 --> 00:26:02,996
Aw, you're the best.
Did you get the coffee?

508
00:26:04,693 --> 00:26:05,912
[Bosco]
'Rebecca?'

509
00:26:05,999 --> 00:26:08,131
- You okay?
- A-okay, boss.

510
00:26:11,047 --> 00:26:12,179
[gunshot]

511
00:26:13,789 --> 00:26:15,748
[gunshot]

512
00:26:15,835 --> 00:26:16,966
Rebecca.

513
00:26:17,053 --> 00:26:18,881
[gunshot]

514
00:26:18,968 --> 00:26:20,187
[Bosco groaning]

515
00:26:22,755 --> 00:26:23,886
[gunshot]

516
00:26:25,192 --> 00:26:26,236
[groaning]

517
00:26:39,162 --> 00:26:40,816
Red John says hi.

518
00:26:40,903 --> 00:26:42,035
[gunshot]

519
00:27:02,708 --> 00:27:05,058
[whispers]
Hi, boss.

520
00:27:05,145 --> 00:27:06,407
[whispers]
Boss.

521
00:27:12,021 --> 00:27:13,109
Hey.

522
00:27:15,329 --> 00:27:16,504
[Lisbon]
Don't move. Drop it now.

523
00:27:16,591 --> 00:27:17,853
[Rebecca grunts]

524
00:27:20,029 --> 00:27:21,770
[Lisbon]
'Bitch.'

525
00:27:21,857 --> 00:27:23,554
You bitch.

526
00:27:23,642 --> 00:27:27,254
Don't move, don't breathe
and don't you smile at me.

527
00:27:28,559 --> 00:27:30,344
[Rebecca chuckles]

528
00:27:33,564 --> 00:27:35,828
What the hell's
with all the balloons?

529
00:27:39,570 --> 00:27:42,008
What are you guys doing here?

530
00:27:42,095 --> 00:27:43,792
[Lisbon]
'Get her outta here.'

531
00:28:03,203 --> 00:28:05,466
[helicopter whirring]

532
00:28:18,348 --> 00:28:20,699
[instrumental music]

533
00:28:23,266 --> 00:28:24,659
[indistinct radio chatter]

534
00:28:33,276 --> 00:28:34,408
[Rebecca sighs]

535
00:28:40,196 --> 00:28:42,590
[music continues]

536
00:28:45,593 --> 00:28:46,725
[Jane sighs]

537
00:28:58,824 --> 00:29:00,869
How long are they
gonna sit there?

538
00:29:00,956 --> 00:29:02,088
Shh.

539
00:29:07,310 --> 00:29:10,270
What's your
favorite kind of music?

540
00:29:10,357 --> 00:29:12,751
Mr. Jane, please.

541
00:29:14,056 --> 00:29:16,058
I know your games.

542
00:29:16,145 --> 00:29:18,539
You don't care
what type of music I like.

543
00:29:18,626 --> 00:29:21,977
I was just making conversation.
Getting to know you.

544
00:29:22,064 --> 00:29:23,457
Well, you want
to know how I could do

545
00:29:23,544 --> 00:29:25,328
such terrible things
for Red John.

546
00:29:25,415 --> 00:29:27,548
Oh, I know that stuff.

547
00:29:27,635 --> 00:29:31,813
Unhappy childhood, sexually
abused by a close relative.

548
00:29:31,900 --> 00:29:34,381
'Cutting or some other
self-abuse.'

549
00:29:35,991 --> 00:29:38,428
Self-medicating,
self-loathing, blah, blah.

550
00:29:38,515 --> 00:29:43,869
E-everyone you ever met
made you feel ashamed.

551
00:29:43,956 --> 00:29:48,351
Ashamed of that ugly darkness

552
00:29:48,438 --> 00:29:51,006
festering inside you.

553
00:29:51,093 --> 00:29:53,487
But he didn't.
He made you strong.

554
00:29:53,574 --> 00:29:55,794
He made you feel
proud of that darkness.

555
00:29:57,621 --> 00:29:58,971
Yes, he did.

556
00:29:59,058 --> 00:30:01,234
'He gave your life
purpose and meaning'

557
00:30:01,321 --> 00:30:04,541
and, uh, love.

558
00:30:04,628 --> 00:30:06,761
[Rebecca]
'And you're very much
like him, you know.'

559
00:30:06,848 --> 00:30:09,111
The way you look at people
and see right through them.

560
00:30:09,198 --> 00:30:10,896
That is just spooky.

561
00:30:14,464 --> 00:30:17,293
I want you to think of this
tonight before you go to sleep.

562
00:30:20,993 --> 00:30:24,474
You are nothing to him
but a useful object.

563
00:30:26,302 --> 00:30:28,304
He is not a good man.

564
00:30:28,391 --> 00:30:30,959
You are so wrong.

565
00:30:31,046 --> 00:30:33,701
He is a very good man.

566
00:30:33,788 --> 00:30:35,529
He's on a mission..

567
00:30:35,616 --> 00:30:37,705
...of love and enlightenment.

568
00:30:37,792 --> 00:30:40,577
He tortures and kills women.

569
00:30:40,664 --> 00:30:42,492
[Rebecca]
Don't you see?

570
00:30:42,579 --> 00:30:44,538
Without death..

571
00:30:44,625 --> 00:30:46,583
...there's no life.

572
00:30:46,670 --> 00:30:49,325
[Rebecca]
'Without darkness,
there's no light.'

573
00:30:49,412 --> 00:30:52,198
- Look at you.
- Me?

574
00:30:52,285 --> 00:30:54,983
'Well, until your wife
and your daughter were killed'

575
00:30:55,070 --> 00:30:57,116
'you were blind, weren't you?'

576
00:30:57,203 --> 00:30:59,292
You were living an illusion.

577
00:30:59,379 --> 00:31:01,860
But Red John opened your eyes.

578
00:31:01,947 --> 00:31:04,775
And now you see the world
for what it truly is.

579
00:31:05,907 --> 00:31:08,867
- Oh.
- 'Mm.'

580
00:31:13,262 --> 00:31:15,047
How did you first meet him?

581
00:31:15,134 --> 00:31:17,919
I'm not telling you
anything about him.

582
00:31:18,006 --> 00:31:20,182
You will.

583
00:31:20,269 --> 00:31:23,707
You'll wake up one day
horrified of what you've done..

584
00:31:23,794 --> 00:31:25,274
...and you will
tell me everything.

585
00:31:25,361 --> 00:31:28,364
No, never.
I love Red John.

586
00:31:28,451 --> 00:31:31,063
And he loves me and I will
never betray that trust.

587
00:31:31,150 --> 00:31:33,239
One day.

588
00:31:33,326 --> 00:31:36,111
But I will tell you that
I like all kinds of music.

589
00:31:36,198 --> 00:31:37,678
Especially country.

590
00:31:37,765 --> 00:31:40,072
And I have a cat named Rex.

591
00:31:40,159 --> 00:31:42,596
And I collect porcelain frogs.

592
00:31:42,683 --> 00:31:45,468
Don't ask me why.
It's just a quirk really.

593
00:31:45,555 --> 00:31:48,080
Well, the psychologist
will want to talk to you next.

594
00:31:48,167 --> 00:31:49,908
He'll have
a field day with that.

595
00:31:49,995 --> 00:31:52,736
But I'm as sane
and as healthy as can be.

596
00:31:54,303 --> 00:31:57,045
- I really am.
- I know.

597
00:31:57,132 --> 00:31:59,395
I do have one question
before you go, Rebecca.

598
00:31:59,482 --> 00:32:03,965
After you took Carter Peak's
body and all the DNA samples..

599
00:32:04,052 --> 00:32:06,750
...why did Red John have
you attack Bosco's team?

600
00:32:08,578 --> 00:32:10,145
There was really no need.

601
00:32:10,232 --> 00:32:13,932
- The evidence was destroyed.
- You know why.

602
00:32:14,019 --> 00:32:17,152
- No.
- 'Oh, you don't?'

603
00:32:17,239 --> 00:32:18,893
Oh, Red John thought
you'd understand.

604
00:32:20,808 --> 00:32:23,593
I got rid
of Bosco and his team..

605
00:32:23,680 --> 00:32:25,508
...so that you could
have the case back.

606
00:32:27,815 --> 00:32:30,470
'Red John misses you.'

607
00:32:30,557 --> 00:32:35,127
And...it's what you wanted too.

608
00:32:35,910 --> 00:32:37,042
'Isn't it?'

609
00:32:52,666 --> 00:32:53,754
We're done here.

610
00:32:55,060 --> 00:32:56,191
[door opens]

611
00:32:59,194 --> 00:33:01,457
Very interesting
talking to you, Rebecca.

612
00:33:01,544 --> 00:33:04,156
Likewise.

613
00:33:04,243 --> 00:33:06,375
I guess I'll see you around.

614
00:33:06,462 --> 00:33:07,637
Yeah.

615
00:33:16,733 --> 00:33:19,040
[Peter Bradley Adam
singing "Darkening Sky"]

616
00:33:30,573 --> 00:33:33,011
[no audio]

617
00:33:36,275 --> 00:33:41,280
♪ Oh come with me
forever my love ♪

618
00:33:41,367 --> 00:33:45,284
♪ Under the darkening sky ♪

619
00:33:45,371 --> 00:33:47,851
♪ Come hide with me ♪

620
00:33:47,938 --> 00:33:50,202
♪ I'll save you my love ♪

621
00:33:50,289 --> 00:33:54,467
♪ Hear me I beg for your life ♪

622
00:34:03,302 --> 00:34:05,782
♪ Her hair is damp ♪

623
00:34:05,869 --> 00:34:08,002
♪ Her skin has turned cold ♪

624
00:34:08,089 --> 00:34:12,137
♪ There's hardly
a sound as she bleeds ♪

625
00:34:12,224 --> 00:34:14,835
♪ Oh stay my love ♪

626
00:34:14,922 --> 00:34:16,837
♪ Please open your eyes ♪

627
00:34:16,924 --> 00:34:20,536
♪ And promise me
you'll never leave ♪

628
00:34:20,623 --> 00:34:24,279
♪ Oh my love ♪

629
00:34:29,241 --> 00:34:33,375
♪ Stay my love.. ♪♪

630
00:34:35,203 --> 00:34:36,813
[indistinct radio chatter]

631
00:34:36,900 --> 00:34:39,686
[man on radio]
'Prisoner is down. She's down.'

632
00:34:47,041 --> 00:34:48,651
Don't touch her!

633
00:34:54,527 --> 00:34:56,746
[panting]

634
00:35:00,750 --> 00:35:01,925
He poisoned her.

635
00:35:18,725 --> 00:35:20,161
[indistinct]

636
00:35:26,689 --> 00:35:28,126
[ECG machine beeping]

637
00:35:28,213 --> 00:35:31,041
Mandy. You get a hold of her?

638
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:33,827
[Lisbon]
'All the flights
out of Boston were delayed.'

639
00:35:33,914 --> 00:35:36,395
'She's in the air now.'

640
00:35:36,482 --> 00:35:39,746
She'll be here soon.
It's alright.

641
00:35:39,833 --> 00:35:41,704
You're gonna be okay.

642
00:35:41,791 --> 00:35:43,706
It's gonna be okay.

643
00:35:43,793 --> 00:35:44,968
Teresa.

644
00:35:47,145 --> 00:35:48,407
Don't lie to me.

645
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:52,715
I can tell when you're lying.

646
00:35:52,802 --> 00:35:54,195
You are.

647
00:35:54,282 --> 00:35:56,241
Look, you will be.
You'll be okay.

648
00:35:57,981 --> 00:35:59,461
I'm a cop.

649
00:36:00,680 --> 00:36:03,161
You're a bad liar.

650
00:36:03,248 --> 00:36:05,772
Your eyes give you
away every time.

651
00:36:05,859 --> 00:36:07,861
Honest eyes.

652
00:36:07,948 --> 00:36:08,905
Sam.

653
00:36:09,863 --> 00:36:11,256
Tell me the truth.

654
00:36:11,343 --> 00:36:12,474
[Lisbon sighs]

655
00:36:16,913 --> 00:36:18,785
You lost a lot of blood.

656
00:36:20,569 --> 00:36:22,441
The doctors don't think
you're gonna make it.

657
00:36:25,792 --> 00:36:28,969
I'm gonna say it, then.

658
00:36:29,056 --> 00:36:31,406
The doctors better be right.

659
00:36:33,147 --> 00:36:34,888
I love you, Teresa.

660
00:36:37,978 --> 00:36:39,719
I love you, too.

661
00:36:40,981 --> 00:36:43,157
No. I mean, I love you.

662
00:36:43,244 --> 00:36:45,203
I know what you mean.

663
00:36:50,251 --> 00:36:52,514
It had to be said.

664
00:37:01,393 --> 00:37:02,742
Is Jane here?

665
00:37:05,179 --> 00:37:10,750
[Bosco]
'For the record,
I'm very pissed off about this.'

666
00:37:10,837 --> 00:37:12,317
Can't blame you.

667
00:37:14,406 --> 00:37:17,800
- Sam, uh--
- We don't have time to be nice.

668
00:37:19,498 --> 00:37:22,022
Red John makes mistakes.

669
00:37:22,109 --> 00:37:25,199
This proves it.
You will catch him.

670
00:37:25,286 --> 00:37:26,244
Yes, I will.

671
00:37:27,680 --> 00:37:29,812
Do me a favor.

672
00:37:29,899 --> 00:37:33,512
When you catch him,
don't arrest him.

673
00:37:33,599 --> 00:37:35,905
Kill the son of a bitch.

674
00:37:35,992 --> 00:37:37,820
That's the plan.

675
00:37:37,907 --> 00:37:39,082
Good.

676
00:37:40,562 --> 00:37:42,129
Listen.

677
00:37:43,739 --> 00:37:45,132
Listen.

678
00:37:51,269 --> 00:37:53,096
[whispers indistinctly]

679
00:37:56,535 --> 00:37:57,971
[ECG machine
beeping erratically]

680
00:37:58,058 --> 00:37:59,102
Bosco?

681
00:38:02,715 --> 00:38:03,672
Bosco?

682
00:38:05,457 --> 00:38:06,588
Sam.

683
00:38:06,675 --> 00:38:08,764
[machine flat lining]

684
00:38:29,742 --> 00:38:32,701
- You weren't at the funeral.
- I was there.

685
00:38:32,788 --> 00:38:35,269
I stayed in the back.

686
00:38:35,356 --> 00:38:37,706
You're quitting?

687
00:38:37,793 --> 00:38:39,926
I tried to
tell you before, but..

688
00:38:41,362 --> 00:38:44,496
Anyway, I prefer retiring.

689
00:38:44,583 --> 00:38:45,888
Full pension.

690
00:38:45,975 --> 00:38:48,195
I got my 20 and then some.

691
00:38:48,282 --> 00:38:50,023
Okay, then.

692
00:38:50,110 --> 00:38:51,720
We'll stay here
and catch the bad guys

693
00:38:51,807 --> 00:38:53,853
while you go fishing.

694
00:38:57,247 --> 00:38:59,902
Lisbon,
in my eight years as SAC

695
00:38:59,989 --> 00:39:03,428
I've lost four agents,
all of them this week.

696
00:39:03,515 --> 00:39:06,169
You should've just quit
last week. It's too late now.

697
00:39:06,256 --> 00:39:08,128
No.

698
00:39:08,215 --> 00:39:09,956
It's time.

699
00:39:12,437 --> 00:39:13,960
You, uh, you take care
of your people.

700
00:39:14,047 --> 00:39:15,527
They're good kids.

701
00:39:17,050 --> 00:39:18,181
Keep an eye on Jane.

702
00:39:18,268 --> 00:39:21,794
If he screws up
too bad, shoot him.

703
00:39:21,881 --> 00:39:25,145
There's not a court in the land
that would convict you.

704
00:39:33,414 --> 00:39:34,502
Mm.

705
00:39:37,287 --> 00:39:38,637
[clears throat]

706
00:39:40,552 --> 00:39:41,640
[sighs]

707
00:39:51,040 --> 00:39:52,259
Hey.

708
00:39:52,346 --> 00:39:53,391
Hey.

709
00:39:55,001 --> 00:39:56,959
I heard about Minelli.

710
00:40:00,267 --> 00:40:01,399
I'm sorry.

711
00:40:04,314 --> 00:40:05,272
Jane..

712
00:40:07,056 --> 00:40:09,058
...you and Bosco..

713
00:40:09,145 --> 00:40:10,059
...at the hospital..

714
00:40:11,974 --> 00:40:13,889
...what'd he say?

715
00:40:13,976 --> 00:40:15,891
Well, he, uh..

716
00:40:19,808 --> 00:40:21,462
He told me to
look after you.

717
00:40:25,118 --> 00:40:26,162
That's all?

718
00:40:26,249 --> 00:40:27,425
No.

719
00:40:30,079 --> 00:40:31,385
He said that
if I didn't look after you

720
00:40:31,472 --> 00:40:33,039
he'd come back and haunt me.

721
00:40:35,041 --> 00:40:36,564
Total nonsense, of course.

722
00:40:36,651 --> 00:40:40,481
But, uh, it wasn't
the right time to correct him.

723
00:40:40,568 --> 00:40:42,178
Tequila?

724
00:40:42,265 --> 00:40:43,441
Bosco's favorite.

725
00:40:51,144 --> 00:40:52,493
Pint of scotch,
left of the fridge

726
00:40:52,580 --> 00:40:53,929
top shelf,
behind the ramen.

727
00:40:54,016 --> 00:40:55,191
Yeah.

728
00:40:56,889 --> 00:40:58,804
To Sam Bosco.

729
00:40:58,891 --> 00:41:00,893
A damn fine agent.

730
00:41:10,729 --> 00:41:12,034
It was a nice service.

731
00:41:14,167 --> 00:41:15,429
Nice music.

732
00:41:15,516 --> 00:41:16,996
Not a fan of the bagpipes.

733
00:41:17,083 --> 00:41:19,781
[Grace]
'Really? I love 'em.'

734
00:41:19,868 --> 00:41:23,655
They're so...lonely.

735
00:41:23,742 --> 00:41:25,874
It was a nice service.

736
00:41:25,961 --> 00:41:28,573
[Rigsby humming
"Amazing Grace"]

737
00:41:32,533 --> 00:41:38,060
♪ Amazing grace ♪

738
00:41:38,147 --> 00:41:43,152
♪ How sweet the sound ♪

739
00:41:43,239 --> 00:41:48,375
♪ That saved a wretch ♪

740
00:41:48,462 --> 00:41:51,813
♪ Like me ♪♪ Like me ♪

741
00:41:51,900 --> 00:41:56,818
♪ I once was lost ♪

742
00:41:56,905 --> 00:42:01,780
♪ But now am found ♪

743
00:42:01,867 --> 00:42:08,526
♪ Was blind but now I see ♪♪

744
00:42:10,919 --> 00:42:13,313
[instrumental music]

745
00:42:20,276 --> 00:42:21,451
[sighs]

746
00:42:40,427 --> 00:42:42,821
[music continues]

747
00:42:53,701 --> 00:42:56,312
[male narrator]
Stay tuned for scenes
from our next episode.

748
00:42:59,315 --> 00:43:01,056
[theme music]

